 "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type I plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/28a3f0e1eda23169a649276a9cde34d3d96cdd75d5b2bc71c3535604612526e5.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=15{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot 15{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}15{x}^{2}{y}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}15{x}^{2}{y}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}{y}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{2}{5}{y}^{5/2}]}_{y={x}^{2}}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{2}(1-|x{|}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{2}(1-{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{2}-6{x}^{7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{3}-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{8}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(2-\\frac{3}{4})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362923 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362924 13194139535715 true] [17592186362923 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362925 13194139535715 true] [17592186362923 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362926 13194139535715 true] [17592186362923 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362927 13194139535715 true] [17592186362923 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362928 13194139535715 true] [17592186362923 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535715 true] [17592186362923 1041 "selection" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362923 1104 #edb/ref 17592186362927 13194139535715 true] [17592186362923 1110 #uuid "2a03178a-4268-539b-aa8a-a11837c1e21f" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362924 1034 "\\frac{7}{2}" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362924 1103 #ed