ion-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/ddc11fc93f034c3d650854e21f178716c941c18f12eb94123e1af2c835c47981.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=2y.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot 2y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}2xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}2y\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot [{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(x-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362958 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362959 13194139535715 true] [17592186362958 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362960 13194139535715 true] [17592186362958 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362961 13194139535715 true] [17592186362958 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362962 13194139535715 true] [17592186362958 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362963 13194139535715 true] [17592186362958 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535715 true] [17592186362958 1041 "selection" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362958 1104 #edb/ref 17592186362963 13194139535715 true] [17592186362958 1110 #uuid "0e4d7a73-4760-5532-9c83-7513aad5616c" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362959 1034 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362959 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535715 true] [17592186362959 1111 #uuid "1394733e-b18b-5759-90c3-a87afe348b55" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362960 1034 "2" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362960 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535715 true] [17592186362960 1111 #uuid "57e8d47e-b539-564a-a9b1-c543480c1661" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362961 1034 "1" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362961 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535715 true] [17592186362961 1111 #uuid "547cb537-a74e-5423-a1eb-7ddc8cd52abe" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362962 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362962 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535715 true] [17592186362962 1111 #uuid "a210b849-0b42-51e7-b227-24416b7ad9d3" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362963 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362963 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535715 true] [17592186362963 1111 #uuid "d1f44364-49e4-5be4-9ef8-2f70fbfa0b27" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362964 1017 #edb/ref 17592186362965 13194139535715 true] [17592186362964 1089 "q-163166" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362964 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535715 true] [17592186362964 1100 "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,{e}^{-y}\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 3}$ and has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{xy}.$ Given that the mass of the lamina is $2$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{y}?$" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362964 1113 #uuid "5f651953-b627-59da-a03c-bc3501f0957b" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362964 1145 "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $m={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot \\frac{1}{xy}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{{e}^{-y}}^{1}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{x={e}^{-y}}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}0-(-y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}=\\frac{4}{2}=2.\n$$" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362965 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362966 13194139535715 true] [17592186362965 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362967 13194139535715 true] [17592186362965 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362968 13194139535715 true] [17592186362965 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362969 13194139535715 true] [17592186362965 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362970 13194139535715 true] [17592186362965 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535715 true] [17592186362965 1041 "selection" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362965 1104 #edb/ref 17592186362967 13194139535715 true] [17592186362965 1110 #uuid "148c3c7d-6b33-5c7f-af4d-1eb6722ca0d1" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362966 1034 "\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362966 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535715 true] [17592186362966 1111 #uuid "1469d538-e53e-5b3c-acd0-d0455ee7e0f0" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362967 1034 "2" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362967 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535715 true] [17592186362967 1111 #uuid "6426b621-0d7d-5eb7-b00b-0811b8418747" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362968 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362968 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535715 true] [17592186362968 1111 #uuid "8b027d77-9abc-503b-9edb-d3f55e6a4619" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362969 1034 "\\frac{5}{4}" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362969 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535715 true] [17592186362969 1111 #uuid "8f77452d-bcd7-59c8-9215-46f297b26fa2" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362970 1034 "\\frac{9}{4}" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362970 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535715 true] [17592186362970 1111 #uuid "0722bafd-e61b-5ed8-9635-1c4d92c23f93" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362971 1017 #edb/ref 17592186362972 13194139535715 true] [17592186362971 1089 "q-163281" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362971 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535715 true] [17592186362971 1100 "Consider a thin plate $D$ that has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}$ and is enclosed between the curve $y={x}^{3}$ and the $x$-axis for $1\\le x\\le 2.$ Given that the mass of the plate is $2$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{x}?$" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362971 1113 #uuid "6536c486-21ee-5d79-a4c6-aa5c7c74e471" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362971 1145 "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $m={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/b6e8af58b8e7ba5f909d226b895bb39b3fc94e53686e4718eb32c9bb4ee61c08.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{3}}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}.$ \n\nSince we require the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $y$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot \\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot [y]_{y=0}^{y={x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{2}]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =4-1 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m}=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362972 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362973 13194139535715 true] [17592186362972 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362974 13194139535715 true] [17592186362972 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362975 13194139535715 true] [17592186362972 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362976 13194139535715 true] [17592186362972 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362977 13194139535715 true] [17592186362972 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535715 true] [17592186362972 1041 "selection" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362972 1104 #edb/ref 17592186362975 13194139535715 true] [17592186362972 1110 #uuid "6ceb42f7-0c98-5500-8b1d-df0e02ace7ac" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362973 1034 "\\frac{7}{5}" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362973 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535715 true] [17592186362973 1111 #uuid "d418d0a4-c635-5fb3-82b2-725ec21e4149" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362974 1034 "\\frac{4}{3}" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362974 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535715 true] [17592186362974 1111 #uuid "62260333-4d07-5577-8af5-954bade7532f" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362975 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362975 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535715 true] [17592186362975 1111 #uuid "6c8e20a8-7f64-5c34-80d3-e9a90d2e4c58" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362976 1034 "\\frac{5}{4}" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362976 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535715 true] [17592186362976 1111 #uuid "0332b99f-b11d-5969-a2d0-2f5dae65e286" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362977 1034 "\\frac{9}{8}" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362977 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535715 true] [17592186362977 1111 #uuid "cf6d5ead-9fe7-51aa-ac9c-7f1ec2271e19" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362978 1017 #edb/ref 17592186362979 13194139535715 true] [17592186362978 1089 "q-163282" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362978 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535715 true] [17592186362978 1100 "Consider a thin plate $D$ that has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=x+y$ and is enclosed between the curve $x=2y$ and the $y$-axis for $0\\le y\\le 1.$ Given that the mass of the plate is $\\frac{4}{3}$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{x}?$" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362978 1113 #uuid "5123abff-afdd-5163-80ce-cbbc07bf474a" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362978 1145 "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $m={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/3097e540292efd601743ba8de24acffc3b51469e77561b2bccbd799d1125e1ed.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2y,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=x+y.$ \n\nSince we require the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $y$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot (x+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}+xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}{x}^{2}+xy\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{{x}^{2}y}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{8{y}^{3}}{3}+2{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{14{y}^{3}}{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{7{y}^{4}}{6}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{7}{6})}{(\\frac{4}{3})}=\\frac{7}{8}.\n$$" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362979 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362980 13194139535715 true] [17592186362979 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362981 13194139535715 true] [17592186362979 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362982 13194139535715 true] [17592186362979 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362983 13194139535715 true] [17592186362979 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362984 13194139535715 true] [17592186362979 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535715 true] [17592186362979 1041 "selection" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362979 1104 #edb/ref 17592186362980 13194139535715 true] [17592186362979 1110 #uuid "7dd2c7f9-6e71-53f2-b63e-4b30ffaf127a" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362980 1034 "\\frac{7}{8}" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362980 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535715 true] [17592186362980 1111 #uuid "8ec69487-9385-55af-ae17-27029770f4b6" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362981 1034 "1" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362981 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535715 true] [17592186362981 1111 #uuid "31420013-9dac-5cfe-9d04-5679c8eac38c" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362982 1034 "\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362982 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535715 true] [17592186362982 1111 #uuid "e75a7462-cbc2-5c43-bf88-24805d6d15d7" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362983 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362983 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535715 true] [17592186362983 1111 #uuid "268a58e9-68ef-50b8-bea7-4f2c6fd9b5ea" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362984 1034 "\\frac{5}{4}" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362984 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535715 true] [17592186362984 1111 #uuid "9f25bd4a-e20a-5611-ba97-dc5e3dce9c83" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362985 1017 #edb/ref 17592186362986 13194139535715 true] [17592186362985 1089 "q-163284" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362985 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535715 true] [17592186362985 1100 "Consider the thin plate $D$ enclosed between the curve $x=\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}$ and the $x$-axis for $-2\\le y\\le 0.$ Given that the area of the plate is $\\pi ,$ find the $x$-coordinate of its centroid." 13194139535715 true] [17592186362985 1113 #uuid "33a3b781-6acf-5dd0-b7cf-d6ee01942bff" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362985 1145 "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/14c292e8a224b59c143d0e8a57d43b554ce298cd4f44fc2169f516d683e8c35a.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}},\\,-2\\le y\\le 0}\n$$\n\nand ${A}_{D}=\\pi .$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{4-{y}^{2}}{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }{\\int }_{-2}^{0}4-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }{[4y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }[0-(-8+\\frac{8}{3})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535715 true] [17592186362986 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362987 13194139535715 true] [17592186362986 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362988 13194139535715 true] [17592186362986 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362989 13194139535715 true] [17592186362986 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362990 13194139535715 true] [17592186362986 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362991 13194139535715 true] [17592186362986 1040 #ed